From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: ntlanman: the Windows network provider; net use

WNetAddConnection2/3, WNetCancelConnection2 and WNetGetConnection go
through network providers, and Wine had none, so every one failed with
ERROR_NO_NETWORK: "net use H: \\server\share" in a logon script, a program
mapping a drive, Explorer's "Map network drive".

- ntlanman.dll, the "Microsoft Windows Network" provider (the Lanman
  workstation's, registered in wine.inf as on Windows): NPGetCaps,
  NPAddConnection/3, NPCancelConnection, NPGetConnection. Its Unix side asks
  Stained Glass OS's sg-netmountd to mount a share with the signed-in user's
  own Kerberos ticket and map a drive letter to it (patch 0056 makes the
  letter visible to that user's programs). Explicit credentials are not
  supported yet: the connection is always made as the signed-in user.
- mpr's WNetGetConnection asks the providers about a remote drive the mount
  manager does not know.
- net.exe: NET USE [device:] \\computer\share[\dir] and NET USE device:
  /DELETE (it could only list connections before).

